1
00:00:28,349 --> 00:00:32,820
RAIDERS

2
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:17,825
The natives are nearby.

3
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:23,931
The poison is still fresh.
Three days. They're following us.

4
00:02:24,265 --> 00:02:28,169
If they knew we were here,
they'd have killed us already.

5
00:02:40,448 --> 00:02:43,885
SOUTH AMERICA
1936

6
00:03:53,354 --> 00:03:57,024
This is the place. Forrestal died here.

7
00:03:57,358 --> 00:04:00,728
- A friend of yours?
- A competitor. He was good.

8
00:04:01,996 --> 00:04:07,702
- He was very, very good.
- No one's ever come out of there alive!

9
00:04:07,835 --> 00:04:09,337
Please.

10
00:05:16,938 --> 00:05:19,807
Stop! Stay out of the light.

11
00:05:42,463 --> 00:05:43,965
It's Forrestal.

12
00:06:30,511 --> 00:06:33,881
Hurry! There's nothing to fear here.

13
00:06:35,816 --> 00:06:37,752
That's what scares me.

14
00:06:56,103 --> 00:06:59,040
- Stay here.
- If you insist.

15
00:08:25,993 --> 00:08:28,863
- Give me the whip!
- Throw me the idol!

16
00:08:30,898 --> 00:08:34,568
There's no time to argue.
Throw me the idol and I'll throw you the whip!

17
00:08:34,702 --> 00:08:37,238
The whip!

18
00:10:03,224 --> 00:10:09,663
Dr. Jones, once again
I take what you possess.

19
00:10:09,797 --> 00:10:12,133
And you thought
I had given up.

20
00:10:22,710 --> 00:10:27,214
You choose your friends poorly.
This time it will cost you dearly.

21
00:10:29,383 --> 00:10:34,421
Too bad the natives don't know you
as well as I do, Belloq.

22
00:10:34,755 --> 00:10:40,861
That's right. You could warn them
if you spoke their language.

23
00:11:27,975 --> 00:11:31,045
Jock! Start the engines! Hurry!

24
00:11:35,049 --> 00:11:39,253
Jock! Start the engines!

25
00:12:28,869 --> 00:12:31,805
There's a huge snake in here!

26
00:12:31,939 --> 00:12:35,075
That's Reggie, my pet.

27
00:12:35,209 --> 00:12:38,312
I hate snakes! I hate them!

28
00:12:38,445 --> 00:12:41,482
Come on, don't be such a coward.

29
00:12:57,998 --> 00:13:01,568
"Neo" means new...

30
00:13:01,902 --> 00:13:06,306
...and "lithic" means stone.

31
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:09,576
Let's return to the burial mound near Hazelton.

32
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:14,415
It contains a passageway
and three chambers or crypts.

33
00:13:19,586 --> 00:13:22,089
This is not a case of theft...

34
00:13:22,222 --> 00:13:26,226
...which would imply that the mound
was stripped of its contents.

35
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:32,866
This site also illustrates
a great danger in archaeology.

36
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,370
Not a physical one,
although that can happen too.

37
00:13:36,503 --> 00:13:38,906
I'm talking about folklore.

38
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:44,078
According to tradition,
a golden coffin was buried here.

39
00:13:44,211 --> 00:13:47,347
Which explains
the number of excavations...

40
00:13:47,481 --> 00:13:49,483
...and the poor condition of what was found.

41
00:13:49,616 --> 00:13:52,486
Chamber three was untouched.

42
00:13:52,619 --> 00:13:55,889
This chamber and the objects found...

43
00:13:56,023 --> 00:13:58,058
...in another one allow us to determine...

44
00:13:59,426 --> 00:14:00,427
I LOVE YOU

45
00:14:03,063 --> 00:14:07,201
...the date of the discoveries.

46
00:14:08,969 --> 00:14:11,004
Any questions?

47
00:14:11,138 --> 00:14:14,007
Well, that's all for today.

48
00:14:15,042 --> 00:14:19,446
Don't forget, Michaelson, chapters four and five
for next class.

49
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:23,217
I'll be in my office on Thursday,
but not Wednesday.

50
00:14:32,226 --> 00:14:35,929
I had it, Marcus. I held it in my hand.

51
00:14:36,063 --> 00:14:37,931
- What happened?
- Take a guess.

52
00:14:39,633 --> 00:14:41,935
- Belloq?
- Want to hear about it?

53
00:14:42,069 --> 00:14:45,139
No. I know everything you do
for the museum...

54
00:14:45,272 --> 00:14:48,509
...complies with the International Treaty
for the Protection of Antiquities.

55
00:14:48,642 --> 00:14:50,544
It's beautiful. And I know how to get it back.

56
00:14:50,677 --> 00:14:54,481
He can only sell it in Marrakesh.
I need $2,000.

57
00:14:54,615 --> 00:14:57,184
Listen. I've brought some people
who want to see you.

58
00:14:57,317 --> 00:15:03,190
I got these pieces.
They're good. Take a look.

59
00:15:03,323 --> 00:15:07,161
The museum will buy them, as always.
No questions asked. They're lovely.

60
00:15:07,294 --> 00:15:11,231
- They're worth a ticket to Marrakesh.
- They're waiting for you.

61
00:15:11,365 --> 00:15:13,967
- Who?
- They're from Intelligence.

62
00:15:14,101 --> 00:15:17,438
They knew you were back before I did.
They know everything.

63
00:15:17,571 --> 00:15:21,475
- They didn't say what they wanted.
- Why would I see them?

64
00:15:21,608 --> 00:15:23,377
Am I in trouble?

65
00:15:23,677 --> 00:15:26,346
Dr. Jones, we've heard of you.

66
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,048
Really?

67
00:15:28,182 --> 00:15:32,119
You're a professor of archaeology,
an expert on the occult.

68
00:15:32,252 --> 00:15:36,356
And, how shall I put it,
a "getter" of rare antiquities.

69
00:15:36,490 --> 00:15:39,460
Have a seat. You'll be more comfortable.

70
00:15:41,028 --> 00:15:44,298
You have a great many talents.

71
00:15:44,431 --> 00:15:48,469
Did you study under Ravenwood
at the University of Chicago?

72
00:15:48,602 --> 00:15:53,307
- That's right.
- Any idea where he is now?

73
00:15:55,442 --> 00:15:58,378
Only rumors.
Somewhere in Asia, I think.

74
00:15:58,512 --> 00:16:02,983
We haven't spoken in ten years.
We were friends...

75
00:16:03,116 --> 00:16:06,520
...but we had a falling-out.

76
00:16:06,653 --> 00:16:12,226
Dr. Jones, you should know that
this is strictly confidential.

77
00:16:12,359 --> 00:16:13,994
I understand.

78
00:16:15,496 --> 00:16:19,032
Yesterday afternoon,
our European section...

79
00:16:19,166 --> 00:16:22,035
...intercepted a German communiqué...

80
00:16:22,169 --> 00:16:24,638
...sent from Cairo to Berlin.

81
00:16:24,771 --> 00:16:29,643
For two years the Nazis
have had teams of archaeologists...

82
00:16:29,776 --> 00:16:32,613
...searching for all kinds
of religious artifacts.

83
00:16:32,746 --> 00:16:37,584
Hitler is fanatical about it.
He's obsessed with the occult.

84
00:16:37,718 --> 00:16:41,755
Right now there's
a German archaeological dig...

85
00:16:42,089 --> 00:16:44,124
...in the desert near Cairo.

86
00:16:44,258 --> 00:16:48,428
We can't decipher this message,
but perhaps you can.

87
00:16:49,463 --> 00:16:52,533
"The exploration team in Tanis...

88
00:16:52,666 --> 00:16:56,270
...seeks to acquire
the headpiece to the Staff of Ra...

89
00:16:57,037 --> 00:16:59,306
...from Abner Ravenwood, U.S.A."

90
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,409
The Nazis have found Tanis.

91
00:17:02,543 --> 00:17:05,612
What does Tanis mean to you?

92
00:17:05,746 --> 00:17:09,483
The Lost Ark may be there.

93
00:17:09,616 --> 00:17:11,084
The Lost Ark?

94
00:17:11,218 --> 00:17:12,452
The Ark of the Covenant.

95
00:17:12,586 --> 00:17:15,155
The Hebrews kept the tablets
of the Law inside it.

96
00:17:15,289 --> 00:17:19,826
- You mean the Ten Commandments?
- Yes, the Ten Commandments.

97
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:24,164
The original tablets Moses brought down
from Mount Sinai and smashed...

98
00:17:24,298 --> 00:17:26,800
...if you believe in that sort of thing.

99
00:17:27,134 --> 00:17:28,702
Didn't you study this?

100
00:17:30,771 --> 00:17:33,307
The Hebrews kept the fragments
in the Ark...

101
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,841
...and when they reached Canaan...

102
00:17:35,175 --> 00:17:37,344
...they placed the Ark
in Solomon's Temple.

103
00:17:37,477 --> 00:17:38,512
In Jerusalem.

104
00:17:38,645 --> 00:17:42,583
It stayed there for many years.
Then suddenly it disappeared.

105
00:17:42,716 --> 00:17:45,452
- Where?
- No one knows where or when.

106
00:17:45,586 --> 00:17:49,656
One of Egypt's pharaohs
invaded Jerusalem...

107
00:17:49,790 --> 00:17:51,625
...around 980 B.C.

108
00:17:51,758 --> 00:17:54,761
Perhaps he took the Ark
to the city of Tanis...

109
00:17:55,095 --> 00:17:58,632
...and hid it in a chamber
called the "Well of Souls."

110
00:17:59,833 --> 00:18:03,503
One year after
the pharaoh returned to Egypt...

111
00:18:03,637 --> 00:18:06,640
...the desert swallowed
the city of Tanis...

112
00:18:06,773 --> 00:18:09,343
...in a sandstorm
that lasted an entire year.

113
00:18:10,377 --> 00:18:12,679
Destroyed by the wrath of God.

114
00:18:16,283 --> 00:18:21,288
I see we were right to come here.
You know everything about Tanis.

115
00:18:21,421 --> 00:18:24,758
No. Actually,
Ravenwood is the expert.

116
00:18:24,891 --> 00:18:29,363
He was the first to investigate Tanis.
He collected its relics.

117
00:18:29,863 --> 00:18:33,767
It was his obsession.
But he never found the city.

118
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:37,404
To tell the truth,
we're suspicious of Mr. Ravenwood.

119
00:18:37,537 --> 00:18:39,740
An American mentioned
so prominently...

120
00:18:39,873 --> 00:18:41,308
...in a secret Nazi communiqué.

121
00:18:41,441 --> 00:18:46,279
- Ravenwood isn't a Nazi!
- Why do the Nazis want him?

122
00:18:46,413 --> 00:18:50,217
Obviously the Nazis are looking
for the headpiece to the Staff of Ra...

123
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:52,386
...and they believe Abner has it.

124
00:18:52,519 --> 00:18:55,255
What exactly is the Staff of Ra?

125
00:18:55,389 --> 00:18:58,225
It's a staff... I don't know, about this long.

126
00:18:58,358 --> 00:19:00,560
No one knows for certain
how long it is.

127
00:19:02,362 --> 00:19:04,931
It's topped with an elaborate piece...

128
00:19:05,265 --> 00:19:08,535
...shaped like the sun,
with a crystal in the center.

129
00:19:08,669 --> 00:19:11,405
You take this staff...

130
00:19:11,538 --> 00:19:12,939
...into a special chamber in Tanis...

131
00:19:13,273 --> 00:19:16,243
...with a miniature of the city
laid out on the floor.

132
00:19:16,376 --> 00:19:19,279
Placed at a certain spot
at a certain time of day...

133
00:19:19,413 --> 00:19:24,251
...the sunlight passes through here
and strikes here.

134
00:19:24,951 --> 00:19:27,954
At the exact location
of the Well of Souls.

135
00:19:28,288 --> 00:19:32,659
- Where the Ark was kept?
- Which is what the Nazis are after.

136
00:19:32,793 --> 00:19:35,262
What does the Ark look like?

137
00:19:36,930 --> 00:19:39,866
There's a drawing of it right here.

138
00:19:43,704 --> 00:19:45,372
Here it is.

139
00:19:52,279 --> 00:19:56,216
- Good God!
- Yes. That's what the Hebrews thought.

140
00:19:57,350 --> 00:19:59,720
What's that coming out of it?

141
00:19:59,853 --> 00:20:04,825
Lightning, fire, the power of God.

142
00:20:07,728 --> 00:20:10,297
I'm beginning to understand Hitler's interest.

143
00:20:11,698 --> 00:20:16,236
The Bible speaks of the Ark leveling
mountains and laying waste to whole regions.

144
00:20:17,704 --> 00:20:21,475
An army that carries the Ark before it...

145
00:20:21,608 --> 00:20:22,976
...is invincible.

146
00:20:43,563 --> 00:20:45,899
You did it, didn't you?

147
00:20:46,032 --> 00:20:49,736
They want you to go.

148
00:20:49,870 --> 00:20:52,839
They want you to get the Ark
before the Nazis do...

149
00:20:52,973 --> 00:20:54,941
...and they'll pay you well.

150
00:20:55,275 --> 00:20:57,577
And the museum gets the Ark in the end.

151
00:20:57,711 --> 00:20:58,879
Of course.

152
00:21:03,383 --> 00:21:07,320
- The Ark of the Covenant.
- Nothing else comes close to it.

153
00:21:08,488 --> 00:21:12,025
This is why we got into archaeology.

154
00:21:15,996 --> 00:21:20,567
Five years ago, I'd have gone myself.
I envy you.

155
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:24,504
I have to find Abner.
I know where to start looking.

156
00:21:29,709 --> 00:21:32,879
- Will she still be with him?
- Possibly.

157
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:37,884
But Marion is the least
of your worries, believe me.

158
00:21:38,018 --> 00:21:39,820
What do you mean?

159
00:21:39,953 --> 00:21:42,722
I mean that for almost 3,000 years...

160
00:21:42,856 --> 00:21:45,592
...mankind has been searching
for the Lost Ark.

161
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:49,663
It's not something to be taken lightly.

162
00:21:50,730 --> 00:21:52,833
No one knows its secrets.

163
00:21:54,835 --> 00:21:57,938
You've never gone after anything like this.

164
00:21:58,772 --> 00:22:02,676
Are you trying to scare me?
You sound like my mother.

165
00:22:02,809 --> 00:22:07,714
We've known each other a long time.
I'm not superstitious.

166
00:22:07,848 --> 00:22:12,886
I'm going after something of
enormous historical significance.

167
00:22:13,019 --> 00:22:16,056
Besides, you know I'm careful.

168
00:22:26,533 --> 00:22:28,635
Good to see you, Dr. Jones.

169
00:25:28,615 --> 00:25:30,583
Hello, Marion.

170
00:25:36,856 --> 00:25:38,958
Indiana Jones.

171
00:25:41,928 --> 00:25:45,799
I knew you'd come back here someday.

172
00:25:45,932 --> 00:25:49,869
I never doubted it. It was inevitable.

173
00:25:50,003 --> 00:25:52,739
What are you doing here in Nepal?

174
00:25:52,872 --> 00:25:55,675
I need one of your father's artifacts.

175
00:25:55,809 --> 00:25:58,678
I've learned to hate you these past ten years.

176
00:26:00,046 --> 00:26:01,247
I never meant to hurt you.

177
00:26:01,581 --> 00:26:05,685
I was a child. I loved you.
You knew what you did was wrong!

178
00:26:05,819 --> 00:26:09,923
- You knew what you were doing.
- I do now! Get out!

179
00:26:13,226 --> 00:26:17,997
Even if you're angry with me,
maybe we can help each other.

180
00:26:19,666 --> 00:26:21,601
Your father collected a bronze disk...

181
00:26:21,734 --> 00:26:25,038
...like this, with a crystal in the middle.

182
00:26:25,171 --> 00:26:29,375
- Do you know which one?
- Yes, I do.

183
00:26:29,709 --> 00:26:32,712
Where's Abner? Where is he?

184
00:26:33,947 --> 00:26:35,348
Abner is dead.

185
00:26:40,220 --> 00:26:45,658
- I'm sorry, Marion.
- You know you ruined my life?

186
00:26:45,792 --> 00:26:50,230
- I've already told you I'm sorry.
- Well, say it again.

187
00:26:50,363 --> 00:26:53,766
- I'm sorry.
- Yeah, everyone's sorry.

188
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:57,003
Abner was sorry for dragging me
into his searches.

189
00:26:57,136 --> 00:26:59,973
I'm sorry I'm still stuck in this dump.

190
00:27:00,707 --> 00:27:02,775
Everybody's sorry about something.

191
00:27:02,909 --> 00:27:06,112
It's a worthless bronze medallion.
Will you give it to me?

192
00:27:06,246 --> 00:27:07,280
Maybe...

193
00:27:07,413 --> 00:27:11,751
- I don't know where it is.
- Maybe you can find it.

194
00:27:12,852 --> 00:27:14,654
Three thousand dollars.

195
00:27:15,989 --> 00:27:19,893
That would get me home,
but not first class.

196
00:27:20,026 --> 00:27:23,763
And another $2,000 in the States.
It's important.

197
00:27:25,431 --> 00:27:27,000
Believe me.

198
00:27:28,668 --> 00:27:32,405
Do you know which piece it is?
Do you know where it is?

199
00:27:35,041 --> 00:27:38,278
- Come back tomorrow.
- Why?

200
00:27:39,012 --> 00:27:41,281
Because I said so. That's why.

201
00:27:49,923 --> 00:27:52,926
See you tomorrow, Indiana Jones.

202
00:29:00,393 --> 00:29:03,963
- Good evening, Fräulein.
- The bar is closed.

203
00:29:04,297 --> 00:29:08,935
We're not... we're not thirsty.

204
00:29:09,902 --> 00:29:13,873
- What do you want?
- The same thing Dr. Jones wants.

205
00:29:14,007 --> 00:29:18,411
Surely he told you
there would be other interested parties.

206
00:29:18,544 --> 00:29:20,813
It must have slipped his mind.

207
00:29:21,247 --> 00:29:23,549
That man is an abomination.

208
00:29:25,285 --> 00:29:28,888
For your sake,
I hope he hasn't acquired it.

209
00:29:29,022 --> 00:29:35,428
- Are you prepared to offer me more?
- Oh, almost certainly. Do you still have it?

210
00:29:41,868 --> 00:29:45,305
No. But I know where it is.

211
00:29:47,206 --> 00:29:49,842
How about a drink for everyone?

212
00:29:49,976 --> 00:29:53,980
Your fire is going out.

213
00:29:55,014 --> 00:29:57,950
Why don't you tell me
where the artifact is?

214
00:29:58,084 --> 00:30:03,523
Listen, mister, I don't know
what kind of people you deal with...

215
00:30:04,924 --> 00:30:07,393
...but nobody gives me orders
in my bar.

216
00:30:07,527 --> 00:30:13,466
Fräulein Ravenwood, allow me
to show you how I deal with people.

217
00:30:17,103 --> 00:30:20,039
Get your hands off me!

218
00:30:21,974 --> 00:30:24,844
Get those filthy hands off me!

219
00:30:30,883 --> 00:30:33,219
Wait. I can be reasonable.

220
00:30:33,353 --> 00:30:36,422
- It's too late for that.
- You don't need that!

221
00:30:38,991 --> 00:30:40,193
Wait.

222
00:30:41,561 --> 00:30:43,496
I'll tell you everything.

223
00:30:43,629 --> 00:30:46,933
Yes... I know you will.

224
00:30:53,473 --> 00:30:55,508
Let her go!

225
00:32:09,482 --> 00:32:11,050
The whiskey!

226
00:32:19,559 --> 00:32:22,562
Kill them. Kill them both!

227
00:33:17,583 --> 00:33:19,285
My medallion!

228
00:33:26,559 --> 00:33:31,230
Well, Jones, you still know
how to show a lady a good time.

229
00:33:31,364 --> 00:33:33,799
- You're unbelievable!
- Am I?

230
00:33:34,133 --> 00:33:35,735
Until I get my $5,000...

231
00:33:36,068 --> 00:33:38,104
...you're going to get even more.

232
00:33:38,237 --> 00:33:40,506
I'm going to be your partner!

233
00:34:18,477 --> 00:34:20,513
Cairo! The city of the living.

234
00:34:20,646 --> 00:34:22,615
Paradise on Earth!

235
00:34:25,451 --> 00:34:28,721
What's all this commotion? What's happening?

236
00:34:28,854 --> 00:34:31,457
And what's this animal?

237
00:34:33,693 --> 00:34:35,561
No!

238
00:34:38,497 --> 00:34:41,367
He's an adorable creature.

239
00:34:43,469 --> 00:34:45,471
Then he's welcome here.

240
00:34:45,605 --> 00:34:48,574
No, don't keep him here on my account.

241
00:34:56,215 --> 00:34:58,684
I knew the Germans would hire you.

242
00:34:58,818 --> 00:35:01,153
You're the best digger in Egypt.

243
00:35:01,287 --> 00:35:04,757
They don't care about that.

244
00:35:04,890 --> 00:35:07,226
They hired every digger in Cairo.

245
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:09,462
The excavation is enormous.

246
00:35:10,529 --> 00:35:13,332
They want strong men
and they pay next to nothing.

247
00:35:14,433 --> 00:35:16,702
Like the old pharaohs.

248
00:35:16,836 --> 00:35:19,872
- And the map room?
- They found it three days ago.

249
00:35:20,206 --> 00:35:23,509
But they're clumsy. Except for one...

250
00:35:24,477 --> 00:35:27,546
...who's very clever.
A French archaeologist.

251
00:35:29,215 --> 00:35:31,884
- What's his name?
- They call him Bellosh.

252
00:35:38,557 --> 00:35:40,626
Belloq? Belloq?

253
00:35:41,594 --> 00:35:44,597
The Germans have
a huge head start on us.

254
00:35:44,730 --> 00:35:47,266
They're close to discovering
the Well of Souls.

255
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:50,403
Well, they won't find it without this.

256
00:35:52,505 --> 00:35:55,307
Who can decipher these markings for us?

257
00:35:56,942 --> 00:35:59,545
I know someone who can help us.

258
00:36:01,847 --> 00:36:06,352
Indy, there's something worrying me.

259
00:36:07,219 --> 00:36:08,621
What is it?

260
00:36:10,322 --> 00:36:11,524
The Ark.

261
00:36:12,258 --> 00:36:17,897
If it is there, in Tanis,
no man should disturb it.

262
00:36:18,230 --> 00:36:22,535
It is surrounded by death.
It is not of this world.

263
00:36:23,569 --> 00:36:26,372
- Do we need the monkey?
- You surprise me.

264
00:36:26,505 --> 00:36:28,808
Talking about our baby like that!

265
00:36:29,508 --> 00:36:32,545
- He has your features.
- And your brains.

266
00:36:33,979 --> 00:36:37,416
I noticed. He's a smart little fellow.

267
00:36:40,419 --> 00:36:44,523
- Hey! Where are you going?
- He'll come back. Have a date.

268
00:36:48,961 --> 00:36:51,597
Come on. Come on, Marion.

269
00:36:51,731 --> 00:36:55,401
- What's this?
- A date. You eat it.

270
00:37:44,884 --> 00:37:48,921
Why don't you have a family,
like your friend Sallah?

271
00:37:49,054 --> 00:37:50,923
Who says I don't?

272
00:37:52,358 --> 00:37:55,361
Me! Dad saw right through you long ago.

273
00:38:04,637 --> 00:38:07,506
- He said you were a bum.
- How generous.

274
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:11,577
The most talented student he ever trained.
He loved you like a son.

275
00:38:11,710 --> 00:38:14,847
- But you managed to wear out his patience.
- Because of you.

276
00:38:32,932 --> 00:38:35,734
Marion, get out of here! Duck!

277
00:39:17,843 --> 00:39:19,411
Of course!

278
00:40:30,849 --> 00:40:33,552
Indy, over here!

279
00:40:33,686 --> 00:40:35,921
Make way!

280
00:40:37,523 --> 00:40:39,058
Help me!

281
00:40:43,996 --> 00:40:47,132
You can't do this to me!
I'm an American! Over here, Indy!

282
00:40:52,604 --> 00:40:56,508
Indiana Jones! Help me! Jones!

283
00:41:17,229 --> 00:41:19,131
- Jones!
- Marion!

284
00:41:22,768 --> 00:41:25,237
Indy!

285
00:41:36,048 --> 00:41:37,983
EXPLOSIVES

286
00:42:06,945 --> 00:42:08,280
Marion...

287
00:43:14,646 --> 00:43:16,915
Did you want to see me?

288
00:43:25,290 --> 00:43:28,026
- Belloq.
- Good afternoon, Dr. Jones.

289
00:43:28,160 --> 00:43:32,231
- I should kill you right now.
- Murder me in public?

290
00:43:33,699 --> 00:43:36,201
These people don't care.

291
00:43:36,335 --> 00:43:39,738
They won't interfere.

292
00:43:39,872 --> 00:43:42,274
I didn't drag the girl into this.

293
00:43:42,407 --> 00:43:44,409
Sit down before you fall down.

294
00:43:44,743 --> 00:43:47,713
Let's behave like civilized people.

295
00:43:58,323 --> 00:44:01,660
You are consistent
in your choice of friends.

296
00:44:01,793 --> 00:44:06,365
It's strange to end this way,
after so many stimulating encounters.

297
00:44:06,698 --> 00:44:08,333
I almost regret it.

298
00:44:08,667 --> 00:44:11,937
Where will I find
another adversary of my caliber?

299
00:44:12,070 --> 00:44:14,006
In the sewer.

300
00:44:16,408 --> 00:44:22,281
You and I are very much alike.
Archaeology is our religion...

301
00:44:22,414 --> 00:44:26,451
...but we've both sinned
against it.

302
00:44:26,785 --> 00:44:30,088
Our methods aren't
so different.

303
00:44:30,222 --> 00:44:33,325
I am your shadowy reflection.

304
00:44:33,458 --> 00:44:36,328
It would take just one step
to make you like me.

305
00:44:36,461 --> 00:44:40,432
- To take you out of the light.
- Now you're being insulting.

306
00:44:42,301 --> 00:44:46,138
You know it's true. How delightful.

307
00:44:46,271 --> 00:44:50,342
Look at this. It's worthless.

308
00:44:50,475 --> 00:44:52,878
You can buy it in the street for $10.

309
00:44:53,011 --> 00:44:57,849
I bury it in the sand for a thousand years
and it becomes priceless.

310
00:44:57,983 --> 00:45:04,089
Like the Ark. Some would kill
for it. Men like you and me.

311
00:45:04,222 --> 00:45:07,926
What about your master, the Führer?

312
00:45:08,060 --> 00:45:11,330
I thought he expected to take possession of it.

313
00:45:11,463 --> 00:45:16,134
In due time.
When I'm finished with it.

314
00:45:16,268 --> 00:45:19,738
Jones, do you understand what the Ark is?

315
00:45:19,871 --> 00:45:24,776
It's a transmitter.
A radio for speaking to God.

316
00:45:24,910 --> 00:45:26,979
And it's within my reach!

317
00:45:28,313 --> 00:45:30,382
You want to talk to God?

318
00:45:32,050 --> 00:45:35,487
Let's go see him together.
I have nothing better...

319
00:45:36,855 --> 00:45:39,224
Uncle Indy, let's go home! Come on!

320
00:45:43,762 --> 00:45:47,933
Next time, the children
won't save you.

321
00:46:04,483 --> 00:46:08,553
They're more effective
than the Marines, huh?

322
00:46:19,064 --> 00:46:23,335
- Marion is dead.
- Yes, I know. I'm sorry.

323
00:46:24,870 --> 00:46:28,407
Life goes on, Indy. That's the truth.

324
00:46:32,177 --> 00:46:36,248
I've got a lot to tell you.

325
00:46:36,381 --> 00:46:38,984
Let's go home and then see the old man.

326
00:47:29,067 --> 00:47:31,269
I don't understand how Belloq did it.

327
00:47:31,403 --> 00:47:33,438
Where did he find a copy of the piece?

328
00:47:33,572 --> 00:47:37,075
There are no illustrations or duplicates.

329
00:47:37,209 --> 00:47:39,478
I saw it with my own eyes. An identical piece.

330
00:47:39,611 --> 00:47:43,615
With a less polished rim.

331
00:47:43,949 --> 00:47:45,984
In the center it had a crystal...

332
00:47:46,118 --> 00:47:52,357
...and around the crystal, on one side,
there were markings like these.

333
00:47:55,227 --> 00:47:57,329
Have they been in the map room?

334
00:47:57,462 --> 00:48:01,233
This morning,
Belloq and the German Dietrich...

335
00:48:02,601 --> 00:48:06,238
...came out and gave us
a new place to excavate.

336
00:48:06,371 --> 00:48:08,273
Farther away.

337
00:48:09,508 --> 00:48:13,512
- The Well of Souls, huh?
- Hey! Look, look at this!

338
00:48:15,113 --> 00:48:18,984
- Sit down. Come on, sit down.
- What is it?

339
00:48:20,619 --> 00:48:25,157
A warning against disturbing
the Ark of the Covenant.

340
00:48:25,290 --> 00:48:28,193
The height of the staff,
did Belloq get it from there?

341
00:48:28,326 --> 00:48:34,299
Yes. Here it is. In the ancient language
this means six kadam high.

342
00:48:34,432 --> 00:48:36,368
- About six feet?
- Wait!

343
00:48:39,538 --> 00:48:46,311
Subtract one kadam, in honor
of the Hebrew God whose Ark it is.

344
00:48:58,590 --> 00:49:03,061
Theirs only had markings
on one side? Are you sure?

345
00:49:04,396 --> 00:49:08,667
Belloq's staff is too long.
They're digging in the wrong place.

346
00:49:11,303 --> 00:49:16,274
I'm the monarch of the sea!
I'm the ruler of the land!

347
00:49:26,618 --> 00:49:28,320
Bad dates.

348
00:49:43,668 --> 00:49:48,106
I told him not to rush
to report it to Berlin.

349
00:49:48,240 --> 00:49:54,145
Archaeology isn't an exact science.
You can't give precise dates.

350
00:49:54,279 --> 00:49:59,484
The Führer is impatient.
He demands constant reports.

351
00:49:59,618 --> 00:50:02,220
- And he expects progress! You said...
- Nothing!

352
00:50:02,354 --> 00:50:04,589
I only said things looked very promising!

353
00:50:04,723 --> 00:50:09,661
Based on our information,
my calculations were correct.

354
00:50:09,794 --> 00:50:11,763
They're not joking, are they?

355
00:50:13,365 --> 00:50:17,435
- What time does the sun hit the map room?
- At nine in the morning.

356
00:50:17,569 --> 00:50:19,404
That's soon.

357
00:50:19,537 --> 00:50:22,674
- Where are they searching for the Well of Souls?
- Over there.

358
00:50:22,807 --> 00:50:25,644
- But the map room is over there.
- Come on, then.

359
00:54:32,724 --> 00:54:34,659
Sallah!

360
00:54:35,593 --> 00:54:37,428
Sallah!

361
00:54:57,549 --> 00:55:01,553
What do you want, my friends? More water?
I'll bring you some.

362
00:55:03,087 --> 00:55:06,357
Do you want more water?
I'll get you more water!

363
00:55:20,538 --> 00:55:24,075
I thought you were dead.
They must have switched the baskets!

364
00:55:28,513 --> 00:55:31,783
- Are you hurt?
- No! Get me out of here.

365
00:55:31,916 --> 00:55:36,454
They'll be back any minute. Untie me!

366
00:55:36,588 --> 00:55:39,424
They keep asking what you know.

367
00:55:43,795 --> 00:55:45,997
What's going on? Untie me!

368
00:55:46,130 --> 00:55:49,000
- I know where the Ark is.
- It's here?

369
00:55:49,934 --> 00:55:52,437
Then I'm coming with you! Get me out!

370
00:55:52,570 --> 00:55:55,740
They'd search the whole place for us.

371
00:55:55,873 --> 00:55:59,677
You have to get me out of here!
Are you crazy?

372
00:56:00,678 --> 00:56:04,716
I'm sorry,
but if you don't stay quiet and still...

373
00:56:04,849 --> 00:56:07,619
...everything will fall apart.

374
00:56:07,752 --> 00:56:09,721
I'll come back for you.

375
00:56:57,035 --> 00:56:58,503
There it is.

376
00:56:59,704 --> 00:57:05,443
Perhaps the Ark is in some chamber
we haven't discovered yet.

377
00:57:05,576 --> 00:57:08,546
There's some vital detail we're missing.

378
00:57:08,680 --> 00:57:12,717
- Maybe the girl can help us.
- That's what I think too.

379
00:57:12,850 --> 00:57:15,019
She had the original for years.

380
00:57:15,153 --> 00:57:18,456
She might remember a lot of things,
with the right motivation.

381
00:57:18,589 --> 00:57:21,225
I'm telling you, she knows nothing.

382
00:57:21,559 --> 00:57:25,096
I'm surprised to see you hesitate.
That's not your reputation.

383
00:57:25,229 --> 00:57:28,900
Don't worry. I have just the man
for this kind of work.

384
00:58:58,623 --> 00:59:01,092
Indy! Here! We found the stone!

385
00:59:05,830 --> 00:59:08,633
Clear it off! Find the edges!

386
00:59:25,249 --> 00:59:28,086
Look! See, Indy? Do you see?

387
00:59:28,219 --> 00:59:32,090
- Bring the bars!
- Work together!

388
00:59:33,791 --> 00:59:35,293
Come on, come on! Push!

389
00:59:40,064 --> 00:59:44,602
Lever it up! That's it! Hold it!

390
00:59:52,677 --> 00:59:54,745
Very carefully!

391
01:00:06,124 --> 01:00:07,925
I'm sorry, Indy.

392
01:00:09,794 --> 01:00:13,097
Why is the ground moving?

393
01:00:15,066 --> 01:00:17,068
Give me the torch.

394
01:00:47,298 --> 01:00:51,202
Snakes. Why did it have
to be snakes?

395
01:00:54,906 --> 01:00:58,409
Asps. Very dangerous.

396
01:01:00,178 --> 01:01:02,180
You go down first.

397
01:01:21,265 --> 01:01:25,836
If you run away on foot, it's three weeks
of desert in every direction.

398
01:01:25,970 --> 01:01:27,939
So please, have something to eat.

399
01:01:35,179 --> 01:01:37,281
I must apologize for the rough treatment.

400
01:01:37,415 --> 01:01:42,186
You've kept me without food or water!
What kind of friends do you have?

401
01:01:42,320 --> 01:01:46,824
In this place, and for my work,
they're necessary evils.

402
01:01:46,958 --> 01:01:51,362
They're not my friends. However,
with the right connections...

403
01:01:51,495 --> 01:01:55,733
...even in this part of the world,
one can live in a civilized manner.

404
01:01:57,835 --> 01:02:01,505
- Beautiful.
- I'd very much like to see you wearing it.

405
01:02:04,208 --> 01:02:06,077
I'm sure you would.

406
01:02:10,248 --> 01:02:11,816
Very well.

407
01:02:20,157 --> 01:02:22,927
What is there to drink around here?

408
01:02:24,862 --> 01:02:28,532
We have little time.
They'll soon come to torture you...

409
01:02:28,866 --> 01:02:34,839
...and I won't be able to stop it,
unless you give me something to appease them.

410
01:02:35,906 --> 01:02:42,013
Some information
I can use to protect you.

411
01:02:42,146 --> 01:02:46,517
I've told you everything I know.
I owe Jones nothing.

412
01:02:46,851 --> 01:02:49,287
He only brought me trouble.

413
01:02:55,860 --> 01:02:57,895
Marion, you're beautiful.

414
01:03:02,867 --> 01:03:05,336
I don't think we need company.

415
01:03:09,140 --> 01:03:11,142
Slowly! Slowly!

416
01:03:14,545 --> 01:03:19,183
Lower it! Carefully!

417
01:03:19,317 --> 01:03:21,319
Are you all right?

418
01:03:23,554 --> 01:03:26,524
Easy, boys. Very easy!

419
01:03:46,977 --> 01:03:49,347
I told you it would work!

420
01:04:14,638 --> 01:04:16,607
Sallah, come down here!

421
01:04:36,127 --> 01:04:37,495
You serve it.

422
01:06:32,042 --> 01:06:33,477
Very good.

423
01:06:44,121 --> 01:06:47,024
What is this?

424
01:06:47,157 --> 01:06:51,729
I grew up with it. My family makes it.

425
01:07:20,724 --> 01:07:24,762
Well, I'm going, Belloq.

426
01:07:27,231 --> 01:07:29,300
I'd like you very much...

427
01:07:29,433 --> 01:07:32,803
...under different circumstances.

428
01:07:37,374 --> 01:07:39,343
We meet again, Fräulein.

429
01:07:40,711 --> 01:07:43,514
All you Americans are alike.

430
01:07:45,149 --> 01:07:48,185
You dress up
for the wrong occasions.

431
01:08:19,249 --> 01:08:20,818
Well then...

432
01:08:23,687 --> 01:08:25,723
...what shall we talk about?

433
01:09:43,834 --> 01:09:46,704
Good! Lift it!

434
01:09:46,837 --> 01:09:48,472
Carefully!

435
01:09:50,374 --> 01:09:54,812
- You're as stubborn as the girl.
- You're far too fond of her.

436
01:09:54,945 --> 01:09:58,415
Your archaeological methods
are very primitive to me.

437
01:09:58,549 --> 01:10:03,287
You'd use a bulldozer
to find a teacup.

438
01:10:08,492 --> 01:10:09,760
Wake up your men!

439
01:10:09,893 --> 01:10:13,797
- The torches are going out!
- Get out of here!

440
01:10:34,518 --> 01:10:38,288
- Sallah.
- Hello! Hello!

441
01:10:39,256 --> 01:10:43,360
Dr. Jones,
what are you doing in that dreadful place?

442
01:10:43,494 --> 01:10:45,362
Come down and I'll show you!

443
01:10:45,496 --> 01:10:49,466
Thank you, my friend.
We're very comfortable up here.

444
01:10:49,600 --> 01:10:50,968
Aren't we?

445
01:10:51,301 --> 01:10:54,037
Oh yes, we're comfortable up here.

446
01:10:55,439 --> 01:10:59,543
Once again, Jones! What was
briefly yours is now mine!

447
01:11:00,978 --> 01:11:03,881
What a fitting end to your life.

448
01:11:04,014 --> 01:11:07,885
You'll be a permanent addition
to this archaeological discovery.

449
01:11:08,018 --> 01:11:11,789
In a thousand years,
even you may be worth something!

450
01:11:13,023 --> 01:11:16,794
- You bastard!
- Unfortunately, we must leave.

451
01:11:16,927 --> 01:11:19,396
Berlin awaits our discovery.

452
01:11:19,530 --> 01:11:22,933
But we don't want to leave you alone
in that dreadful place.

453
01:11:23,066 --> 01:11:26,570
Let me go, you wretch! Let me go!

454
01:11:29,606 --> 01:11:30,641
Marion!

455
01:11:34,778 --> 01:11:37,815
Hold on! Don't fall!

456
01:11:42,486 --> 01:11:45,055
You traitor, let me go!

457
01:11:52,663 --> 01:11:54,031
Snakes...

458
01:11:56,567 --> 01:11:58,101
At your feet!

459
01:11:58,435 --> 01:11:59,436
The girl was mine!

460
01:11:59,570 --> 01:12:02,573
She was of no use to us.
Only our mission for the Führer matters.

461
01:12:05,542 --> 01:12:09,613
Sometimes I wonder
if you clearly understand that.

462
01:12:09,746 --> 01:12:14,484
- It didn't work this time.
- You scoundrels will pay for this!

463
01:12:14,618 --> 01:12:17,788
Indiana Jones, adieu.

464
01:12:42,379 --> 01:12:45,148
Here. Wave it at anything
that crawls.

465
01:12:46,550 --> 01:12:48,852
Everything in here crawls!

466
01:12:51,855 --> 01:12:54,691
- Indy!
- Ow!

467
01:12:58,395 --> 01:13:02,766
- Did he give you that dress?
- I tried to escape! Without your help!

468
01:13:02,900 --> 01:13:05,469
- Did you try very hard?
- Where were you?

469
01:13:06,403 --> 01:13:08,939
- What are you doing?
- It'll feed the fire.

470
01:13:11,842 --> 01:13:14,511
- How do we get out?
- I'm thinking about it.

471
01:13:14,645 --> 01:13:16,480
Well, think faster.

472
01:13:22,653 --> 01:13:25,422
- Where are you going?
- Through that wall!

473
01:13:26,156 --> 01:13:30,160
- Get ready to run!
- What do you mean?

474
01:13:42,072 --> 01:13:46,576
Indy! Don't leave me here alone!

475
01:14:12,936 --> 01:14:19,009
- Here we go. Get ready!
- The torch is going out!

476
01:15:00,584 --> 01:15:01,685
Indy?

477
01:15:24,041 --> 01:15:25,876
Marion! Look! Look!

478
01:16:04,781 --> 01:16:09,853
They're taking the Ark by plane.
We'll be on it when they load it.

479
01:16:14,858 --> 01:16:19,696
Monsieur, let's drink to our success.
To the Ark.

480
01:16:19,830 --> 01:16:23,100
When we're far away from here.

481
01:18:27,123 --> 01:18:28,124
Indy!

482
01:19:19,209 --> 01:19:21,411
Stay with the Ark!

483
01:19:27,117 --> 01:19:28,518
Watch out!

484
01:19:39,062 --> 01:19:41,164
- Oh my God!
- Marion!

485
01:19:41,298 --> 01:19:44,200
I can't get out! Get me out!

486
01:19:46,903 --> 01:19:49,139
- It won't open!
- Open it!

487
01:19:53,109 --> 01:19:55,078
I can't get out.

488
01:19:55,211 --> 01:19:58,415
Indy, it's stuck.

489
01:20:28,511 --> 01:20:30,947
- It's stuck.
- Turn it!

490
01:20:31,081 --> 01:20:33,950
- It's stuck!
- Stand back!

491
01:20:55,305 --> 01:20:57,574
Get the Ark out of here!

492
01:20:57,907 --> 01:21:01,177
Put it in the truck.
We'll take a plane from Cairo.

493
01:21:01,311 --> 01:21:04,447
And I want plenty of protection.

494
01:21:10,653 --> 01:21:12,255
Jones!

495
01:21:17,894 --> 01:21:21,931
Good grief, my friends! I'm so glad
you're not dead!

496
01:21:23,233 --> 01:21:28,405
Indy, if you want the Ark,
they're taking it by truck to Cairo.

497
01:21:28,538 --> 01:21:31,508
By truck? Which truck?

498
01:21:59,536 --> 01:22:01,137
Come on!

499
01:22:09,546 --> 01:22:13,216
Go back to Cairo.
Get transportation to England.

500
01:22:13,349 --> 01:22:18,121
Ship, plane, anything.
We'll meet at Omar's.

501
01:22:18,254 --> 01:22:20,323
- I'm going after that truck.
- How?

502
01:22:20,457 --> 01:22:23,293
I don't know.
I'm making it up as I go.

503
01:30:04,453 --> 01:30:07,757
There! Everything's arranged.
The Ark is aboard.

504
01:30:07,890 --> 01:30:10,893
Everything's complete with you,
or what's left of you.

505
01:30:11,027 --> 01:30:13,195
- Do you trust these people?
- Yes.

506
01:30:15,431 --> 01:30:17,033
Mr. Katanga.

507
01:30:20,469 --> 01:30:25,074
These are my friends. My family.

508
01:30:25,207 --> 01:30:28,544
If you don't treat them well, I'll know.

509
01:30:28,678 --> 01:30:30,813
My cabin is theirs.

510
01:30:30,946 --> 01:30:34,684
Mr. Jones!
I've heard so much about you.

511
01:30:35,551 --> 01:30:38,587
You look just as I imagined.

512
01:30:43,059 --> 01:30:44,660
Goodbye.

513
01:30:47,229 --> 01:30:51,100
Take care of each other.
I miss you already.

514
01:30:53,803 --> 01:30:56,005
You're a good friend.

515
01:30:58,107 --> 01:30:59,542
Sallah...

516
01:31:03,112 --> 01:31:05,147
For Fayah.

517
01:31:06,549 --> 01:31:09,685
For your children. And for you.

518
01:31:15,157 --> 01:31:16,726
Thank you.

519
01:31:25,701 --> 01:31:30,873
An English sailor
is a singing soul.

520
01:31:31,006 --> 01:31:35,177
As free as the wind on the mountains.

521
01:31:49,859 --> 01:31:51,560
Where did you go?

522
01:31:51,694 --> 01:31:53,596
I went to wash up.

523
01:31:54,697 --> 01:31:56,866
Where did you get that?

524
01:31:56,999 --> 01:31:59,235
- He gave it to me.
- Who's he?

525
01:31:59,568 --> 01:32:03,572
Katanga. I doubt I'm the first woman
to travel on this ship.

526
01:32:04,106 --> 01:32:07,777
- Very pretty.
- Really?

527
01:32:07,910 --> 01:32:09,278
- Yes.
- Really?

528
01:32:22,691 --> 01:32:24,260
What did you say?

529
01:32:30,833 --> 01:32:33,335
Wait. I don't need any help.

530
01:32:33,669 --> 01:32:34,904
Yes, you do.

531
01:32:37,306 --> 01:32:39,809
You're not the man
I knew ten years ago.

532
01:32:39,942 --> 01:32:43,312
It's not the years, it's the mileage.

533
01:32:51,654 --> 01:32:55,691
- I don't need a nurse.
- Don't be a child.

534
01:32:55,825 --> 01:32:59,094
- Does it hurt?
- That hurts!

535
01:33:00,896 --> 01:33:04,667
Well, where doesn't it hurt?

536
01:33:04,800 --> 01:33:06,035
Here.

537
01:33:12,041 --> 01:33:13,275
Here.

538
01:33:22,284 --> 01:33:24,253
It doesn't hurt so much here.

539
01:33:33,762 --> 01:33:34,897
Here?

540
01:33:55,851 --> 01:33:56,986
Jones?

541
01:33:59,388 --> 01:34:00,723
Jones!

542
01:34:03,726 --> 01:34:06,262
We never find the right moment, do we?

543
01:34:34,423 --> 01:34:36,926
- What's happening?
- The engines stopped.

544
01:34:37,059 --> 01:34:38,894
I'll go see.

545
01:34:49,338 --> 01:34:51,206
- What's happening?
- Important friends are coming.

546
01:34:54,476 --> 01:34:59,214
You and the girl must disappear.
I'll hide you in the hold.

547
01:35:13,228 --> 01:35:16,932
- Where's Dr. Jones?
- Let me go!

548
01:35:21,737 --> 01:35:23,339
Don't touch me!

549
01:36:08,250 --> 01:36:11,787
- Where is Jones?
- We haven't found him yet.

550
01:36:11,920 --> 01:36:13,389
Jones is dead.

551
01:36:16,258 --> 01:36:20,195
I killed him. He was of no use to us.

552
01:36:20,329 --> 01:36:26,001
The girl has a certain value
where we're going.

553
01:36:29,071 --> 01:36:33,142
Herr Colonel. You take that cargo.

554
01:36:33,275 --> 01:36:37,146
All right. Leave us the girl
as compensation for our losses.

555
01:36:37,279 --> 01:36:42,518
You savage! You're in no position
to demand anything!

556
01:36:42,851 --> 01:36:45,020
We'll take whatever we want.

557
01:36:45,154 --> 01:36:48,323
And then decide
whether to blow up your ship.

558
01:36:50,893 --> 01:36:55,130
The girl comes with me.
She'll be part of my compensation.

559
01:36:55,264 --> 01:36:58,200
I'm sure the Führer will approve.

560
01:36:58,333 --> 01:37:02,071
If she doesn't please me, I'll leave her to you.

561
01:37:02,204 --> 01:37:04,606
I won't waste any more time on her.

562
01:37:04,940 --> 01:37:06,275
Excuse me.

563
01:37:22,357 --> 01:37:25,427
I can't find Mr. Jones.
I've looked everywhere.

564
01:37:25,561 --> 01:37:28,163
He has to be somewhere.

565
01:37:28,297 --> 01:37:29,598
Look again.

566
01:37:31,366 --> 01:37:33,168
- I've found him.
- Where?

567
01:37:33,302 --> 01:37:34,436
There!

568
01:40:00,749 --> 01:40:04,119
The altar is ready,
as you instructed, sir.

569
01:40:04,253 --> 01:40:06,755
Good. Take the Ark
there immediately.

570
01:40:09,358 --> 01:40:10,759
Monsieur...

571
01:40:12,794 --> 01:40:17,366
The thought of this Jewish ritual
makes me uneasy.

572
01:40:19,234 --> 01:40:21,670
Are you certain it's necessary?

573
01:40:21,803 --> 01:40:23,705
Let me ask you this...

574
01:40:24,039 --> 01:40:29,578
...would you rather open the Ark in Berlin
before the Führer...

575
01:40:29,711 --> 01:40:33,815
...without knowing for certain whether
the tablets of the Ten Commandments are inside?

576
01:40:34,149 --> 01:40:37,252
Without knowing whether
you have fulfilled your mission...

577
01:40:37,386 --> 01:40:40,355
...and found
the one true Ark?

578
01:42:12,781 --> 01:42:13,915
Jones?

579
01:42:15,317 --> 01:42:16,451
Jones?

580
01:42:16,585 --> 01:42:19,321
I'll blow up the Ark!

581
01:42:25,227 --> 01:42:27,763
Your persistence surprises
even me!

582
01:42:29,264 --> 01:42:32,801
You're ruining the reputation
of good mercenaries.

583
01:42:36,471 --> 01:42:38,874
You can't expect to escape this island.

584
01:42:39,207 --> 01:42:41,343
That depends on how reasonable we are.

585
01:42:41,476 --> 01:42:43,412
I just want the girl.

586
01:42:48,517 --> 01:42:53,288
- And if we refuse?
- Your Führer won't get the Ark!

587
01:42:54,356 --> 01:42:58,560
All right, move back.
Everybody, step aside!

588
01:42:58,693 --> 01:43:01,263
All right, Jones. You win.

589
01:43:02,798 --> 01:43:04,399
Blow it up!

590
01:43:10,405 --> 01:43:15,210
Yes, blow it up! Blow it sky-high!

591
01:43:16,511 --> 01:43:20,449
You've spent your whole life
searching for archaeological relics.

592
01:43:20,582 --> 01:43:24,920
Inside the Ark are treasures beyond
your wildest dreams.

593
01:43:25,253 --> 01:43:27,756
You want to see it opened as much as I do.

594
01:43:29,491 --> 01:43:33,862
Indiana, we're merely
passing through history.

595
01:43:35,997 --> 01:43:41,403
This... this is history!

596
01:43:51,480 --> 01:43:52,981
Do whatever you want.

597
01:46:28,470 --> 01:46:33,441
Marion, don't look. Close your eyes
and don't look at it, no matter what happens!

598
01:47:02,170 --> 01:47:04,039
It's beautiful!

599
01:47:14,783 --> 01:47:18,119
- Indy?
- Don't look. Keep your eyes shut!

600
01:48:36,598 --> 01:48:37,832
Marion...

601
01:49:10,565 --> 01:49:13,668
You have served your country well,
and we thank you.

602
01:49:13,802 --> 01:49:17,672
We hope you'll find the arrangements satisfactory.

603
01:49:17,806 --> 01:49:20,308
The money, yes.
The situation is unacceptable.

604
01:49:20,642 --> 01:49:25,180
- Well, gentlemen, this matter is closed.
- Where is the Ark?

605
01:49:26,981 --> 01:49:31,686
I thought we'd made that clear.
It's in a very safe place.

606
01:49:31,820 --> 01:49:35,089
- Safe from whom?
- The Ark radiates an unusual power...

607
01:49:35,223 --> 01:49:38,693
- ...and it must be studied.
- And it will be.

608
01:49:38,827 --> 01:49:42,363
You have my assurance, Dr. Brody, Dr. Jones.

609
01:49:42,697 --> 01:49:45,667
Our top men
are working on it right now.

610
01:49:47,202 --> 01:49:51,840
- Who?
- Top men.

611
01:49:55,376 --> 01:49:58,913
What happened? You don't look very happy.

612
01:49:59,047 --> 01:50:01,749
- Fools. Bureaucratic fools!
- What did they say?

613
01:50:02,817 --> 01:50:06,955
- They don't know what they've got there.
- Well, I know what I've got here.

614
01:50:08,756 --> 01:50:11,059
Come on. Let me buy you a drink.

615
01:50:13,328 --> 01:50:15,997
You know... a drink?

616
01:50:39,387 --> 01:50:40,388
TOP SECRET MILITARY
